# Defaults for `act`, so `make ci-local` needs no flags.
#
# act runs jobs in Docker containers that approximate GitHub's runners. It is
# an approximation: OIDC, most of the `github` context, the real cache backend
# and GitHub-hosted service networking are not simulated. Use it to catch shell
# and wiring mistakes in seconds; use a real run to prove the workflow works.

# The default runner image is a stub with almost nothing installed.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Apple Silicon runs amd64 images under emulation. Slower, but matches CI.
--container-architecture linux/amd64

# Without this, upload-artifact fails rather than being skipped.
--artifact-server-path /tmp/act-artifacts
